Title Handbrake Turn <Extended Models>
CATEGORY Extended Models 
DATASET_TITLE Handbrake Turn
#RingCtrl8 1
#RingCtrl9 1

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example simulates the application of a handbrake. Three concepts are illustrated in this example:
#
#1. Using VS Commands to operate the rear brakes only in response to a user-defined control signal (hb_on) to simulate the action of a handbrake.
#
#2. Defining a state variable to implement brake system dynamics (a time constant) in the handbrake application.
#
#3. Implementing the control signal using generic, user-defined table functions.
#
#The hand brake is applied to the rear wheels only and its operation does not cause the brake lights to illuminate.
#
#Click on the Procedures blue link "Handbrake Turn Initialization" and follow the Event series for more information.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

